---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/buyers.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Buying a Home in DuPage County | AJ Tayfel"
  description="Buyer guidance for home purchases throughout DuPage County and Chicago's western suburbs with AJ Tayfel, REALTOR®."
>
  <section class="buyer-hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">For Buyers</p>

        <h1>
          Find the right home.<br />
          Understand the decision.
        </h1>

        <p class="hero-lede">
          Buying well is not just about finding a property you like.
          It is about understanding the market, the property, the numbers,
          and the tradeoffs before you commit.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="primary-button" href="/contact/">
            Start a Buyer Conversation
          </a>

          <a class="secondary-link" href="/communities/">
            Explore Communities →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="buyer-index">
        <p class="index-eyebrow">Buyer Planning</p>

        <div class="index-row">
          <span>01</span>
          <strong>Priorities</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="index-row">
          <span>02</span>
          <strong>Market</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="index-row">
          <span>03</span>
          <strong>Property</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="index-row">
          <span>04</span>
          <strong>Offer</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="index-row">
          <span>05</span>
          <strong>Closing</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="intro-section">
    <div class="container intro-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The Approach</p>

        <h2>
          Start with what matters<br />
          before looking at listings.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="intro-copy">
        <p class="lead">
          A productive home search starts with more than bedrooms, bathrooms,
          and price.
        </p>

        <p>
          Location, taxes, condition, monthly carrying costs, association
          obligations, commute, future resale, and your own timing can all
          change whether a property is actually a good fit.
        </p>

        <p>
          The goal is to define those priorities early so each property can
          be evaluated against a real plan instead of just emotion.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="process-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="process-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Buyer Roadmap</p>

        <h2>
          A clear process from<br />
          search to closing.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="process-list">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>

          <div>
            <h3>Define the search</h3>
            <p>
              Establish the areas, property types, budget, timing, and
              priorities that should guide the search.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>02</span>

          <div>
            <h3>Understand the market</h3>
            <p>
              Review comparable sales, active competition, market pace, and
              what different price points are actually delivering.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>03</span>

          <div>
            <h3>Evaluate the property</h3>
            <p>
              Look beyond finishes and first impressions to condition,
              disclosures, taxes, associations, and property-specific risks.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>04</span>

          <div>
            <h3>Structure the offer</h3>
            <p>
              Consider price alongside financing, contingencies, timing,
              possession, and the strength of the overall terms.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>05</span>

          <div>
            <h3>Manage the transaction</h3>
            <p>
              Keep attorney review, inspection, appraisal, financing, and
              closing milestones coordinated through completion.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="decision-section">
    <div class="container decision-grid">
      <div class="decision-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Look Beyond the Listing Photos</p>

        <h2>
          The details can matter more than the décor.
        </h2>

        <p>
          Two homes with the same asking price can create very different
          ownership experiences and long-term costs.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="decision-list">
        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <strong>Property taxes</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <strong>Condition & maintenance</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <strong>Association obligations</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <strong>Location & commute</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <strong>Resale considerations</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <strong>Transaction timing</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="local-section">
    <div class="container local-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Local Market</p>

        <h2>
          DuPage County & Chicago's western suburbs.
        </h2>

        <p>
          Neighborhood character, housing stock, taxes, amenities, and market
          behavior vary considerably from community to community.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="local-actions">
        <a href="/communities/">
          <span>Explore</span>
          <strong>Local Communities</strong>
          <b>↗</b>
        </a>

        <a href="/contact/">
          <span>Discuss</span>
          <strong>Your Home Search</strong>
          <b>↗</b>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing-section">
    <div class="container closing-inner">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Planning a Purchase?</p>

        <h2>
          Start with the conversation,<br />
          not the showing schedule.
        </h2>

        <p>
          Tell me where you are in the process and what you are hoping to
          accomplish.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="closing-button" href="/contact/">
        Contact AJ
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
